    "description": "ClaimsPortal loads a claim into CaseEditor, where a caseworker may change severity, notes, and assigned queue over several minutes. The portal is deployed in two instances, and both instances can display the same claim revision. When the first caseworker saves, the second caseworker's later save currently overwrites the first change because the update contains only the editable columns. The ClaimRepository must make a stale save detectable and return a conflict response containing the current revision, without holding a database lock while the form is open. Every claim row needs a durable, opaque revision value that changes whenever the row is stored; the value presented in the editor must be checked against the stored value during the update, and an atomic compare-and-set operation must ensure that only one competing save succeeds. This concurrency rule applies independently to each claim and must also cover saves made by the background ClaimAutomationWorker, even when that worker uses a different application service.",
    "decision_statement": "Whether each claim update should be conditioned on the opaque revision supplied when the editor loaded the row, rejecting stale edits instead of overwriting newer data.",
    "notes": "version-number fits the opaque per-row revision with compare-and-set rejecting stale saves; unit-of-work is the transactional-coordination near miss and identity-map supports session identity."
  },
